  "title": "osf: head-stamped PR description blocks, a file table, and a provider retry",
  "summary": "This change reworks how `osf` writes generated blocks into a pull request description. A new `marker` module becomes the single place that knows the marker style `<!-- osf:NAME:start head=<sha> -->` … `<!-- osf:NAME:end -->`, and it also recognises the older markers (`osf:NAME:start` with no head, and the legacy `factory:status:begin/end`), so an open pull request migrates in place on its next write instead of gaining a duplicate block. `osf pr status render` is rewritten around that marker: it drops the Problem/Approach rows and the Ready verdict, and emits a head-stamped heading plus a seven-row Check/Result/Details table (Risk, Tests, CI, Commit messages, Contributor agreement, Automated review, Human review) with collapsed sections for risk reasons, review rounds and test changes. A new `osf pr tree render` command reads the change from git and prints the collapsed file table for the `osf:tree` block, with coloured count chips and log-scale size bars. The pr-lens workflow now resolves up to two providers that hold a key and retries once with the second when the first model call fails, and every `osf pr section write` call passes the pull request's head commit.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
